{"node":{"id":"MONDO:0008995","label":"Yunis-Varon syndrome","definition":"Yunis-Varon syndrome is a rare condition that affects many different parts of the body. Signs and symptoms are generally present from birth and may include underdeveloped or absent collarbones (clavicles); large fontanelles; characteristic facial features; hypotonia (reduced muscle tone) and/or abnormalities of the fingers and toes. Affected people may also experience feeding difficulties, breathing problems, brain malformations, heart defects, skeletal abnormalities, developmental delay, and/or intellectual disability. Yunis-Varon syndrome is caused by changes (mutations) in the FIG4 gene and isinherited in an autosomal recessive manner. Treatment is based on the signs and symptoms present in each person.","synonyms":["YVS","Yunis Varon Syndrome","Yunis Varon syndrome","Yunis-Varón syndrome","cleidocranial dysplasia with micrognathia, absent thumbs, and distal aphalangia","cleidocranial dysplasia-micrognathia-absent thumbs syndrome"],"xrefs":["DOID:0060589","GARD:0000331","MEDGEN:341818","MESH:C536719","NORD:1875","OMIM:216340","Orphanet:3472","UMLS:C1857663","icd11.foundation:1696991249"],"parents":[],"parents_labels":{},"children":[],"children_labels":{},"in_core":false,"cluster_id":null,"is_group":false,"n_genes":2,"n_phenotypes":154,"mechanism_classes":[]},"genes":[{"id":"e_17a2023624a2","source":"MONDO:0008995","target":"FIG4","type":"caused_by","evidence":[{"db":"Orphanet","origin":"Orphanet","record":"ORPHA:3472","level":"curated","date":"2026-06-23","url":"https://www.orpha.net/en/disease/detail/3472","confidence":0.95,"snippet":"Disease-causing germline mutation(s) (loss of function) in (Assessed) — FIG4 phosphoinositide 5-phosphatase"},{"db":"HPO","origin":"Orphanet","record":"ORPHA:3472","level":"curated","date":"2026-09-02","confidence":0.9,"url":"https://hpo.jax.org/browse/disease/ORPHA:3472","snippet":"FIG4 is annotated as disease gene of ORPHA:3472 (HPO genes_to_phenotype, Orp